      {
        "h_title": "Hoy tod recipe tips and tricks",
        "main_title": "Thai Fried Mussels Recipe (Hoi Tod)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Avoid overcrowding: Space is a must for the ultimate puff in your batter! Try cooking just two portions at a time—it’s the best way to get perfect results.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Use fresh seafood: I like to start with fresh, high-quality pre-shelled mussel meat. If you can’t find it fresh, you can use frozen, thawed in the fridge before using.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Storing and reheating tips",
        "main_title": "Thai Fried Mussels Recipe (Hoi Tod)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Storing : Let your leftover Thai mussel pancake cool to room temperature and keep it in an airtight container in the fridge for up to 2 days.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Reheating : To reheat mussels, place them in a hot pan over medium heat until warmed through. This method keeps them tender. Avoid using the microwave!",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Frequently asked questions",
        "main_title": "Thai Fried Mussels Recipe (Hoi Tod)",
        "author": "Praew",
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Are pan-fried mussels spicy?",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Pan-fried mussels can be spicy if you add spicy ingredients like chili peppers. But if you don’t add spicy stuff, they won’t be spicy.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "What to serve with Thai mussels?",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          },
          {
            "text": "Thai mussels can be served with steamed rice or noodles. Adding a fresh salad or some stir-fried vegetables can complete your meal.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
